.. Shared fragment: the out-of-domain rule. Included by every language guide;
   edit here, not in the guides.

Every eval path treats out-of-domain input the same way. The fit covers
``[a, b)``. A point exactly at the upper corner ``b`` returns the boundary
value, the last cell's polynomial. Points below ``a``, points above ``b``, and
``NaN`` or ±Inf inputs all return ``NaN``. The batch path stays branchless,
because the domain test compiles to a SIMD mask.
